[12.31, "o", "\u001b[1m== 2. Logs ==\u001b[0m\r"]
[12.37, "o", "\r\n"]
[12.43, "o", "  \u001b[33m[warn]\u001b[0m /var/log/nginx/access.log: 1 POST(s) to static-file paths\r"]
[12.49, "o", "\r\n"]
[12.55, "o", "         192.0.2.10 - - [20/Oct/2026:21:14:02 +0000] \"POST /favicon.ico HTTP/1.1\" 502 157 \"-\" \"curl/8.5.0\"\r"]
[12.61, "o", "\r\n"]
[12.67, "o", "  \u001b[33m[warn]\u001b[0m /var/log/nginx/access.log: 1 POST(s) answered with 5xx. Top paths:\r"]
[12.73, "o", "\r\n"]
[12.79, "o", "         1\t/favicon.ico\r"]
[12.85, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.2, "o", "  \u001b[31m[FLAG]\u001b[0m /var/log/nginx/error.log: 1 out-of-memory fatal(s) 'in Unknown on line 0' (died while parsing the request)\r"]
[13.26, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.32, "o", "         [20-Oct-2026 21:14:01] PHP Fatal error:  Allowed memory size of 134217728 bytes exhausted (tried to allocate 20480 bytes) in Unknown on line 0\r"]
[13.38, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.73, "o", "  \u001b[31m[FLAG]\u001b[0m /var/log/nginx/error.log: 1 worker crash / heap-corruption line(s)\r"]
[13.79, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.85, "o", "         [20-Oct-2026 21:14:02] WARNING: [pool www] child 41 exited on signal 11 (SIGSEGV) after 12.3 seconds from start\r"]
[13.91, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.97, "o", "  \u001b[33m[warn]\u001b[0m /var/log/nginx/error.log: 1 upstream reset(s): the PHP backend dropped the connection mid-request\r"]
[14.03, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.09, "o", "         2026/10/20 21:14:02 [error] 31#31: *88 upstream prematurely closed connection while reading response header from upstream, client: 192.0.2.10, request: \"POST /favicon.ico HTTP/1.1\"\r"]
[14.15, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.21, "o", "  \u001b[33m[warn]\u001b[0m /var/log/nginx/error.log: 1 input-limit rejection(s) during request parsing\r"]
[14.27, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.33, "o", "         [20-Oct-2026 21:14:03] PHP Warning:  Unknown: Input variable nesting level exceeded 64. To increase the limit change max_input_nesting_level in php.ini. in Unknown on line 0\r"]
[14.39, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.45, "o", "  \u001b[34m[info]\u001b[0m behind a CDN or tunnel, access-log client IPs may all be the proxy's. Your edge's\r"]
[14.51, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.57, "o", "  \u001b[34m[info]\u001b[0m analytics (e.g. Cloudflare GraphQL) can show 5xx and 52x bursts even if logs were lost.\r"]
[14.63, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.69, "o", "\r"]
[14.75, "o", "\r\n"]
[15.35, "o", "\u001b[1m== 3. Sessions ==\u001b[0m\r"]
[15.41, "o", "\r\n"]
[15.76, "o", "  \u001b[31m[FLAG]\u001b[0m /var/lib/php/sessions: 1 of 2 session file(s) contain upload_progress_ data\r"]
[15.82, "o", "\r\n"]
[15.88, "o", "         -rw-r--r--    1 root     root            42 Oct 22 16:23 /var/lib/php/sessions/sess_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\r"]
[15.94, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.0, "o", "  \u001b[33m[warn]\u001b[0m /var/lib/php/sessions: session ids PHP would not generate (odd length or characters):\r"]
[16.06, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.12, "o", "         <demo>\r"]
[16.18, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.24, "o", "  \u001b[34m[info]\u001b[0m /tmp: no PHP session files\r"]
